2.
Definitions. - (a) "Agricultural Marketing Adviser" means the Agricultural Marketing Adviser to the Government of India.
(b)
"authorised packer" means a person to whom or a body of persons to which a certificate of authorisation has been
granted to grade and mark Castor seeds in accordance with the grade standards and procedure provided under these
rules;
(c)
"certificate of authorisation" means a certificate issued under the provisions of the General Grading and Marking Rules,
1988 authorising a perron or a body of persons to grade and mark Castor seeds with the grade designation mark;
(d)
"General Grading and Marking Rules" means the General Grading and Marking Rules, 1988 made under section 3 of
the Agricultural Produce (Grading and Marking) Act, 1937 (1 of 1937);
(e)
"Grade designation mark" means the "Agmark Insignia" referred to in rule 5;
(f)
"Schedule" means a Schedule appended to these rules;
